<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-store-leftovers">How to Store Leftovers?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Leftover burrata caprese will <strong>keep in an airtight container in the fridge for 2&ndash;3 days</strong>. Keep in mind that the burrata&rsquo;s creamy center will solidify a bit over time, so it won&rsquo;t be quite as creamy on days two and three.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before serving leftovers, drain off any excess liquid to prevent them from becoming soggy. To &ldquo;revive&rdquo; your burrata caprese, add a few fresh tomato slices and some fresh basil leaves, then drizzle with a little extra olive oil and balsamic vinegar. Finish with a sprinkle of flaky salt for a fresh, vibrant bite.</p>


