<div id="recipe-67481-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-67481-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="67481"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-67481-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Slice tomatoes into &#8531;-inch thick slices. Arrange them on a serving platter. Sprinkle tomato slices with &frac12; teaspoon salt.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-67481-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Arrange burrata balls in the middle or gently break them with a sharp pairing knife and scatter the chunks over the sliced tomatoes.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-67481-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Sprinkle everything with the rest of the salt and freshly ground black pepper. Drizzle with olive oil and balsamic vinegar.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-67481-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Garnish it with basil leaves. Serve!</div></li></ul></div></div>
